Usage: fno config plugin install [OPTIONS] [HARNESS]

  Install your local checkout for development. --dev replaces a release-channel
  plugin.

  Side effects. It builds a stage under ~/.fno/plugin-stage/fno (fno-pack with
  --pack, which drops the mux skills and mux hooks) and points the harness at
  it. footnote gets a link at ~/.footnote/plugins/fno. It removes stale plugin
  copies. It strips the machine-wide
  CARGO_BUILD_BUILD_DIR and SCCACHE_DIR lines an older install wrote, from
  ~/.zshrc, ~/.bashrc, the Claude settings.json and the Codex config.toml. It
  then runs a reclaim pass over fno's own caches, without the uv cache prune.
  The receipt names every file it rewrote.

Arguments:
  [HARNESS]  claude | codex | opencode | pi | agy | grok | zcode | footnote

Options:
  --pack  Install the pack profile: no mux skills, no mux hooks.
  --help  Show this message and exit.
